          }
        }
      ],
      "themes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "analects.08.19",
      "number": 19,
      "original": {
        "language": "zh",
        "script": "Hant",
        "textType": "classical_chinese",
        "text": "子曰。大哉堯之爲軍也、巍巍乎、唯天爲大、唯堯則之、蕩蕩乎、民無能名焉。巍巍乎、其有成功也、煥乎、其有文章。",
        "source": {
          "title": "The Analects",
          "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
          "citation": "Book 8, passage 19"
        }
      },
      "translations": [
        {
          "id": "analects.08.19.en.muller",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "The Master said: “The rulership of Yao was so magnificent! He was so sublime that even though there is nothing as great as Heaven, he could accord with it. His greatness was so boundless it is beyond description. His efficacy was amazing, his writings were enlightening.”",
          "translator": "A. Charles Muller",
          "source": {
            "title": "The Analects",
            "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
            "citation": "Book 8, passage 19"
          },
          "rights": {
            "reuseStatus": "licensed",
            "license": "User-authorized reuse with attribution required"
          }
        }
      ],
      "commentary": [],
      "themes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "analects.08.20",
      "number": 20,
      "original": {
        "language": "zh",
        "script": "Hant",
        "textType": "classical_chinese",
        "text": "舜有臣五人、而天下治。武王曰。予有亂臣十人。孔子曰。才難、不其然乎、唐虞之際、於斯爲盛、有婦人焉、九人而已。三分天下有其二、以服事殷、周之德、其可謂至德也已矣。",
        "source": {
          "title": "The Analects",
          "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
          "citation": "Book 8, passage 20"
        }
      },
      "translations": [
        {
          "id": "analects.08.20.en.muller",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "Shun, with five ministers, was able to successfully govern the empire. King Wu said, “Altogether I have ten ministers.” Confucius said, “Their ability is the issue. Don't you think so? When the Tang and Wu dynasties combined, they had as many ministers as you, with a woman and nine men. King Wen (of the Zhou) controlled two-thirds of the empire, and with this, served the Yin. Indeed, the virtue of Zhou can be called the epitome of virtue!”",
          "translator": "A. Charles Muller",
          "source": {
            "title": "The Analects",
            "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
            "citation": "Book 8, passage 20"
          },
          "rights": {
            "reuseStatus": "licensed",
            "license": "User-authorized reuse with attribution required"
          }
        }
      ],
      "commentary": [],
      "themes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "analects.08.21",
      "number": 21,
      "original": {
        "language": "zh",
        "script": "Hant",
        "textType": "classical_chinese",
        "text": "子曰。禹吾無間然矣、菲飮食、而致孝乎鬼神、惡衣服、而致美乎黻冕、卑宮室、而盡力乎溝恤、禹吾無間然矣。",
        "source": {
          "title": "The Analects",
          "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
          "citation": "Book 8, passage 21"
        }
      },
      "translations": [
        {
          "id": "analects.08.21.en.muller",
          "language": "en",
          "text": "The Master said: “Yu was flawless in character. Surviving on the simplest food and drink, yet perfect in his piety to the ancestral spirits. Normally wearing coarse clothing, he looked magnificent in his ceremonial cap and gown. Living in a humble abode, he exhausted himself in the excavation of drainage ways and canals. I cannot find a flaw in his character!”",
          "translator": "A. Charles Muller",
          "source": {
            "title": "The Analects",
            "url": "https://www.acmuller.net/con-dao/analects.html",
            "citation": "Book 8, passage 21"
          },
          "rights": {
            "reuseStatus": "licensed",
            "license": "User-authorized reuse with attribution required"
          }
        }
      ],
      "commentary": [],
      "themes": []
    }
  ]
